From: Antonin Kral <A.Kral@sh.cvut.cz>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 15:54:08 +0200
Subject: Fix man(1)/troff warnings in the atari800 manual page

Forwarded: yes
Last-Update: 2026-07-27

The manual page uses tbl(1) tables but lacks the "'\" t" preprocessor
line, so man does not run tbl and the tables are emitted as raw text.
This produces:

  troff: warning: cannot adjust line; underset by 34n
  an.tmac: warning: tbl preprocessor failed, or it or soelim was not run;
           table(s) likely not rendered (TE macro called with TW register
           undefined)

Adding the preprocessor line makes tbl run, which in turn exposes three
tables whose width exactly reaches the available line length (1776u at
the default 80 column terminal), triggering:

  warning: centered table wider than line length minus indentation

Reducing the column separation from the default 3n to 2n for the
right-hand data columns brings the tables inside the available width
while keeping the layout intact.
---
 src/atari800.man | 23 ++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/atari800.man b/src/atari800.man
index 8aa6f0f..3626901 100644
--- a/src/atari800.man
+++ b/src/atari800.man
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+'\" t
 .TH ATARI800 1 "2026-07-26" "Atari800 7.1.2"
 
 .SH NAME
@@ -1831,8 +1832,8 @@ the \fB-compression-level 0\fR command line argument.
